#!/usr/bin/env python3.11
"""push-gate-verify — proves, against the real engine clones on this machine,
that the push content gate (`bin/push-content-gate`, installed as a pre-push
hook by `bin/install-push-gate`) refuses a forbidden name and passes a clean
commit.

WHY A SEPARATE PROGRAM, RUN BY HAND. `tests/test_push_content_gate.py` and
`tests/test_publish_scan.py` already cover the gate's logic end to end, but
only against a fake engine — CI must never read the operator's own private
names, so it cannot be the thing that proves the REAL engine, with the REAL
private-names file, actually refuses a push naming one of them in every clone
where the hook is installed. Only the operator can run this: it is the only
reader of that file, and it is never dispatched or scheduled.

WHAT IT DOES. For each clone install-push-gate knows about
(agent-platform, library, convivy-orient, convivy-deck, write-better) that
carries the installer's marker in `.git/hooks/pre-push`, this prints "<repo>:
probing...", then builds two throwaway commits — one holding a name from the
operator's private-names file, one holding fixed harmless text — and pushes
each to its own fresh temp bare repository, so the clone's OWN installed
hook runs exactly as it would on a real `git push`. The forbidden commit
must be refused (non-zero exit, with its probe path named in the output);
the clean commit is the positive control and must succeed (without it,
"refused" could mean the gate refuses everything). A clone without the
marker is reported as not installed and fails the run.

EACH PROBE COMMIT IS BUILT ON THE CLONE'S OWN HEAD, SO ITS PARENT IS A REAL
COMMIT. A parentless probe's one parent is git's empty-tree sha
(`4b825dc6...`), not a commit, and publish-engine refuses to export a
non-commit — `_scan_added_findings` then reads that as "could not run" and
refuses the probe for a scan that could not run, never for the probe's own
content, so the forbidden probe can never come back refused and the
verifier can never pass (2026-10-26, every installed clone). Parenting each
probe on the clone's HEAD is what gives publish-engine a real commit to
export when it scans the probe's parent.

EACH THROWAWAY BARE REPO IS SEEDED WITH THAT SAME HEAD FIRST, WITHOUT RUNNING
THE HOOK. `_seed_bare_with_head` pushes the clone's HEAD to the bare repo's
`refs/heads/probe` with `--no-verify`, so the clone's own installed hook
never runs for that one push; only the probe commit, pushed to that same ref
right after, fires it. Without this seeding, the probe's bare repo would
have no ref at all when the probe is pushed, and `bin/push-content-gate`'s
own already-known-commits lookup (`publish_scan.commits_new_to_remote`)
would read EVERY commit reachable from the probe — HEAD, and everything
before it — as new to the remote, oldest first, judging the probe not on
its own content but on the clone's entire history, including a commit that
can predate the gate and already carry a finding, the way agent-platform's,
library's and convivy-orient's each did when this was first run (the bug
`test_an_older_refused_commit_in_the_clones_history_is_not_scanned` guards
against). With the bare repo already at HEAD before the probe is pushed,
`git rev-list <probe> --not <head>` names the probe alone.

NEITHER PROBE TOUCHES THE CLONE'S HEAD, INDEX OR WORKING TREE. Each commit is
built with `GIT_INDEX_FILE` pointed at a throwaway temp file that is never
seeded from the clone's own index or HEAD, so the clone's real index is never
read or written; the probe commit itself is created with `git commit-tree
-p <head>`, holding only its own one path, and never attached to any ref in
the clone itself — only, briefly, to `refs/heads/probe` in the throwaway
bare repo it is pushed to. Both probe commits land in the clone's object
store too (git writes an object it is asked to create regardless of what
references it), unreferenced there and reachable only by their own sha, and
stay there until that clone's own `git gc` collects them — they never leave
this machine, since the only remote either is ever pushed to is a temp bare
repository this program creates and deletes before it exits, including when
a probe push times out (below).

A PROBE PUSH THAT HANGS IS REPORTED, NOT WAITED ON FOREVER. Each push to the
temp bare repository is given 300 seconds; a probe that has not finished by
then is reported as not finishing, and the run moves on to the next clone.
Before this, a probe that misbehaved by scanning a clone's entire history
could also take long enough on that history to look, from the operator's
terminal, indistinguishable from having hung for good.

NEVER PRINTS THE PRIVATE NAME. The name taken from the private-names file is
used only as file content inside a probe commit object; it is never put in
any message, exception or line this program prints. Diagnostic output is
filtered to lines naming the probe's own path, the gate's "push refused" /
"nothing was sent" lines, publish-engine's own "publish-engine: ..." report
lines, and lines shaped like one of its findings (leading whitespace, then
`<path>:<line>: <description>`) — never the full output, which could
otherwise carry a crashed publish-engine's own Python traceback unchanged
(`lib/agent-platform/publish_scan.py`'s `_scan_one` puts its stdout and
stderr straight into the refusal message on the "could not run" branch) or
anything else more than this program means to show — and even those are
scrubbed for the name as a second safeguard.

A publish-engine report's finding lines carry everything a reader needs on
their own; its indented section headers are left out of what gets kept for
exactly that reason. A hand scan of agent-platform's oldest commit shows the
shape (no value is printed; this is the report's own text, not a probe's
output):

    publish-engine: agent-platform at <sha> (<short>) would be refused by a
    release. No value is printed; open each file to judge it.
      content scan (66):
        README.md:44: a launchd label outside the product's namespace
        README.md:44: a person's name

Each finding line already names its own path, line and description; the
header above it adds only the category's name and a count, neither of which
a reader needs to make sense of the finding beneath it.

`--root-config FILE` is the test seam the sibling installers share
(company/decisions/0008): it names a `session-agent.env` holding `CREWS_ROOT`
for `bin/builder-root --root` to read instead of this machine's real one.
`--bare-repo-dir DIR` is a second, narrower test seam: it names a directory
this program creates its throwaway bare repositories under instead of the
system temp directory, so a test can make one clone's bare-repo creation
fail without touching the others. `--probe-timeout SECONDS` is a third test
seam: it shortens the 300-second limit each probe push is given, so a test
can make a probe time out without waiting 300 real seconds for it. The
operator calls this program without any of the three; install.sh never calls
this program at all, only `bin/install-push-gate`.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "lib" / "agent-platform"))

import publish_scan as PS  # noqa: E402

# bin/install-push-gate is these two values' source of truth (it is POSIX sh,
# not something this Python program can import); keep this list and marker in
# sync with its CLONES and MARKER by hand if either ever changes there.
CLONES = ("agent-platform", "library", "convivy-orient", "convivy-deck", "write-better")
MARKER = "# managed-by: agent-platform push-gate"

FORBIDDEN_PROBE_PATH = "push-gate-probe/forbidden.txt"
CLEAN_PROBE_PATH = "push-gate-probe/clean.txt"
CLEAN_PROBE_CONTENT = b"push-gate-verify: harmless probe content\n"

# How long a single probe push is given before it is reported as not having
# finished rather than waited on forever — see the module docstring's "A
# PROBE PUSH THAT HANGS" paragraph. `--probe-timeout` (tests only) overrides
# this with a value short enough that a test does not wait 300 real seconds.
DEFAULT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 300

_REDACTED = "[REDACTED]"


class CloneCheckFailed(Exception):
    """One clone's forbidden or clean probe did not behave as required. The
    message is already filtered and scrubbed and is safe to print."""


def _resolve_root(root_config: str | None) -> Path | None:
    builder_root = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "builder-root"
    cmd = [str(builder_root), "--root"]
    if root_config:
        cmd += ["--config", root_config]
    result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)
    if result.returncode != 0:
        return None
    root = result.stdout.strip()
    return Path(root) if root else None


def _first_private_name() -> str:
    """The first non-empty, non-comment line of the operator's private-names
    file — `publish_scan.private_names_file()`'s own resolution, never a
    path this program picks itself. NEVER returned to a caller that might
    print it; used only as probe commit content."""
    path = PS.private_names_file()
    try:
        text = path.read_text()
    except OSError as exc:
        raise RuntimeError(f"cannot read the private names file ({path}): {exc}") from exc
    for line in text.splitlines():
        stripped = line.strip()
        if stripped and not stripped.startswith("#"):
            return stripped
    raise RuntimeError(f"{path} has no non-comment line to use as a forbidden probe")


def _run_git(clone: Path, args: list[str], *, env: dict[str, str] | None = None,
             input_bytes: bytes | None = None) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    result = subprocess.run(
        ["git", "-C", str(clone), *args], env=env, input=input_bytes, capture_output=True,
    )
    if result.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError(
            f"git {' '.join(args)} failed in {clone}: "
            f"{result.stderr.decode(errors='replace').strip()}"
        )
    return result


def _build_probe_commit(clone: Path, probe_rel_path: str, content: bytes,
                         parent_sha: str) -> str:
    """A commit parented on `parent_sha` — the clone's own HEAD, so
    publish-engine can scan a real commit when it scans this probe's parent
    (see the module docstring's "EACH PROBE COMMIT IS BUILT ON THE CLONE'S
    OWN HEAD" paragraph) — whose tree holds exactly one blob, `content` at
    `probe_rel_path`. Built through a throwaway `GIT_INDEX_FILE` that is
    never seeded from `clone`'s own index or HEAD (so `clone`'s real index,
    HEAD and working tree are all untouched) and never attached to any ref
    in `clone` itself."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="push-gate-verify-index-") as tmp_dir:
        index_path = Path(tmp_dir) / "index"
        env = {**os.environ, "GIT_INDEX_FILE": str(index_path)}
        blob_sha = _run_git(
            clone, ["hash-object", "-w", "--stdin"], env=env, input_bytes=content,
        ).stdout.decode().strip()
        _run_git(clone, ["update-index", "--add", "--cacheinfo",
                          f"100644,{blob_sha},{probe_rel_path}"], env=env)
        tree_sha = _run_git(clone, ["write-tree"], env=env).stdout.decode().strip()
        commit_env = {
            **env,
            "GIT_AUTHOR_NAME": "push-gate-verify", "GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL": "push-gate-verify@localhost",
            "GIT_COMMITTER_NAME": "push-gate-verify", "GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL": "push-gate-verify@localhost",
        }
        commit_sha = _run_git(
            clone, ["commit-tree", tree_sha, "-p", parent_sha, "-m", "push-gate probe"],
            env=commit_env,
        ).stdout.decode().strip()
    return commit_sha


def _seed_bare_with_head(clone: Path, head_sha: str, bare: Path,
                          timeout_seconds: float) -> None:
    """Push `head_sha` into `bare`'s `refs/heads/probe`, from `clone` itself,
    with `--no-verify` so `clone`'s own installed pre-push hook never runs
    for this push — only the probe commit pushed to that same ref right
    after is meant to fire it. See the module docstring's "EACH THROWAWAY
    BARE REPO IS SEEDED" paragraph for why skipping this would make the
    probe judged on the clone's entire history instead of on itself.

    Raises `RuntimeError` on a non-zero exit or a push that does not finish
    within `timeout_seconds`, exactly like every other git failure in this
    file (`_run_git`, `_init_bare`) — seeding is this program's own
    infrastructure, never something `_verify_clone`'s forbidden/clean
    reporting should explain."""
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(
            ["git", "-C", str(clone), "push", "--no-verify", f"file://{bare}",
             f"{head_sha}:refs/heads/probe"],
            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout_seconds,
        )
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as exc:
        raise RuntimeError(
            f"git push --no-verify to seed {bare} with {head_sha[:9]} did not "
            f"finish within {timeout_seconds:g} s"
        ) from exc
    if result.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError(
            f"git push --no-verify to seed {bare} with {head_sha[:9]} failed: "
            f"{result.stderr.strip()}"
        )


def _init_bare(path: Path) -> None:
    """`git init --bare` at `path`, raising `RuntimeError` on failure like
    every other git failure in this file — never `CalledProcessError`, so
    `main()`'s per-clone handling reports it and moves on to the next
    clone instead of the whole run dying on one clone's bare-repo
    creation. `path` need not exist yet: git creates it."""
    result = subprocess.run(
        ["git", "init", "-q", "--bare", "-b", "main", str(path)], capture_output=True,
    )
    if result.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError(
            f"git init --bare failed for {path}: "
            f"{result.stderr.decode(errors='replace').strip()}"
        )


def _push_probe(clone: Path, commit_sha: str, bare: Path,
                 timeout_seconds: float) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess | None:
    """Push `commit_sha` to a fresh ref on `bare`, from `clone` itself —
    so `clone`'s own installed `pre-push` hook is the thing that runs,
    exactly as it would on an ordinary `git push` from that clone.

    Returns `None`, rather than waiting any longer, if the push has not
    finished within `timeout_seconds` — see the module docstring's "A PROBE
    PUSH THAT HANGS" paragraph. The pushed-to `bare` repository is still
    removed by `_verify_clone`'s `finally` block in that case; killing the
    timed-out `git push` process is `subprocess.run`'s own behavior on
    `TimeoutExpired`, not something this function does itself."""
    try:
        return subprocess.run(
            ["git", "-C", str(clone), "push", f"file://{bare}", f"{commit_sha}:refs/heads/probe"],
            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout_seconds,
        )
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return None


# A publish-engine finding line's own shape: leading whitespace, then
# `<path>:<line>: ` (the path can hold no whitespace), then a description —
# e.g. "    README.md:44: a launchd label outside the product's namespace".
# Matched by shape alone, never by content, so it catches a finding line
# from any clone's engine report without naming any category in advance;
# that same looseness is exactly why it must NOT match a crashed engine's
# indented traceback lines (a "  File ..." line, or the source line below
# it), which carry no `<path>:<line>:` of their own.
_FINDING_LINE = re.compile(r"^\s+\S+:\d+:\s\S")


def _relevant_lines(output: str, probe_path: str) -> list[str]:
    """Only the lines worth printing: ones naming the probe's own path, the
    gate's own "push refused" / "nothing was sent" lines, publish-engine's
    own "publish-engine: ..." report lines, and lines shaped like one of its
    findings (`_FINDING_LINE`) — never the full output, which could
    otherwise carry a crashed engine's own Python traceback unchanged, or
    anything else more than this program means to show.

    Publish-engine's own indented section headers (e.g. "  content scan
    (66):") are deliberately left out: every finding beneath one already
    names its own path, line and description, so the header's category
    label and count are never needed to read a finding, and a hand scan of
    a real report (this file's module docstring) shows none besides."""
    keep = []
    for line in output.splitlines():
        lowered = line.lower()
        if (
            probe_path in line
            or "push refused" in lowered
            or "nothing was sent" in lowered
            or line.lstrip().startswith("publish-engine:")
            or _FINDING_LINE.match(line)
        ):
            keep.append(line)
    return keep


def _scrub(text: str, private_name: str) -> str:
    """A second safeguard against the private name ever reaching output:
    even though nothing in this program's own messages should carry it, any
    occurrence of it in text taken from a subprocess's output is replaced
    before that text is printed."""
    return text.replace(private_name, _REDACTED) if private_name else text


def _verify_clone(repo: str, clone: Path, private_name: str,
                   bare_repo_dir: Path | None = None,
                   probe_timeout: float = DEFAULT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS) -> None:
    """Raises `CloneCheckFailed` with an already-filtered, already-scrubbed
    message on any failure, and `RuntimeError` if either bare repo cannot
    be created or seeded with the clone's HEAD; returns normally when both
    probes behaved.

    `bare_repo_dir`, when given (the `--bare-repo-dir` test seam), is used
    literally as the parent of this clone's two bare repos rather than a
    fresh directory under the system temp directory, so a test can make
    one clone's bare-repo creation fail without disturbing the others.
    `probe_timeout` (the `--probe-timeout` test seam) is how long each probe
    push is given before it is reported as not finished; see `_push_probe`."""
    if bare_repo_dir is not None:
        forbidden_bare = bare_repo_dir / f"{repo}-forbidden"
        clean_bare = bare_repo_dir / f"{repo}-clean"
    else:
        forbidden_bare = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="push-gate-verify-forbidden-"))
        clean_bare = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="push-gate-verify-clean-"))
    try:
        _init_bare(forbidden_bare)
        _init_bare(clean_bare)

        head_sha = _run_git(clone, ["rev-parse", "HEAD"]).stdout.decode().strip()
        _seed_bare_with_head(clone, head_sha, forbidden_bare, probe_timeout)
        _seed_bare_with_head(clone, head_sha, clean_bare, probe_timeout)

        forbidden_content = f"push-gate-verify forbidden probe: {private_name}\n".encode()
        forbidden_sha = _build_probe_commit(
            clone, FORBIDDEN_PROBE_PATH, forbidden_content, head_sha,
        )
        forbidden_result = _push_probe(clone, forbidden_sha, forbidden_bare, probe_timeout)
        forbidden_timed_out = forbidden_result is None
        forbidden_output = (
            "" if forbidden_timed_out else forbidden_result.stdout + forbidden_result.stderr
        )
        forbidden_ok = (
            not forbidden_timed_out
            and forbidden_result.returncode != 0
            and FORBIDDEN_PROBE_PATH in forbidden_output
        )

        clean_sha = _build_probe_commit(
            clone, CLEAN_PROBE_PATH, CLEAN_PROBE_CONTENT, head_sha,
        )
        clean_result = _push_probe(clone, clean_sha, clean_bare, probe_timeout)
        clean_timed_out = clean_result is None
        clean_output = "" if clean_timed_out else clean_result.stdout + clean_result.stderr
        clean_ok = not clean_timed_out and clean_result.returncode == 0

        if forbidden_ok and clean_ok:
            return

        details = []
        if not forbidden_ok:
            if forbidden_timed_out:
                details.append(
                    f"forbidden probe push did not finish within {probe_timeout:g} s"
                )
            else:
                lines = _relevant_lines(forbidden_output, FORBIDDEN_PROBE_PATH)
                shown = "; ".join(lines) if lines else "(no relevant output)"
                details.append(
                    f"forbidden probe NOT refused (exit {forbidden_result.returncode}): "
                    f"{_scrub(shown, private_name)}"
                )
        if not clean_ok:
            if clean_timed_out:
                details.append(
                    f"clean probe push did not finish within {probe_timeout:g} s"
                )
            else:
                lines = _relevant_lines(clean_output, CLEAN_PROBE_PATH)
                shown = "; ".join(lines) if lines else "(no relevant output)"
                details.append(
                    f"clean probe failed (exit {clean_result.returncode}): "
                    f"{_scrub(shown, private_name)}"
                )
        raise CloneCheckFailed("; ".join(details))
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(forbidden_bare, ignore_errors=True)
        shutil.rmtree(clean_bare, ignore_errors=True)


def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="push-gate-verify",
        description="Prove the push content gate refuses a forbidden name and "
                    "passes a clean commit in every installed clone.",
    )
    ap.add_argument("--root-config", default=None,
                    help="read the machine's root from this session-agent.env "
                         "instead of the real one (tests only)")
    ap.add_argument("--bare-repo-dir", default=None,
                    help="create each clone's throwaway bare repos under this "
                         "directory instead of the system temp directory "
                         "(tests only)")
    ap.add_argument("--probe-timeout", type=float, default=DEFAULT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS,
                    help="give each probe push this many seconds instead of "
                         f"{DEFAULT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:g} before reporting it as "
                         "not finished (tests only)")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv[1:])
    bare_repo_dir = Path(args.bare_repo_dir) if args.bare_repo_dir else None

    root = _resolve_root(args.root_config)
    if root is None:
        print("push-gate-verify: cannot resolve the machine's root "
              "(bin/builder-root --root)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    try:
        private_name = _first_private_name()
    except (RuntimeError, PS.OC.OperatorConfigError) as exc:
        print(f"push-gate-verify: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    overall_ok = True
    for repo in CLONES:
        clone = root / repo
        hook = clone / ".git" / "hooks" / "pre-push"
        if not clone.is_dir() or not hook.is_file():
            print(f"{repo}: not installed (no pre-push hook)")
            overall_ok = False
            continue
        try:
            marker_present = MARKER in hook.read_text(errors="replace")
        except OSError as exc:
            print(f"{repo}: cannot read its pre-push hook: {exc}")
            overall_ok = False
            continue
        if not marker_present:
            print(f"{repo}: not installed (pre-push hook carries no push-gate marker)")
            overall_ok = False
            continue

        print(f"{repo}: probing...", flush=True)
        try:
            _verify_clone(repo, clone, private_name, bare_repo_dir, args.probe_timeout)
        except CloneCheckFailed as exc:
            print(f"{repo}: {exc}")
            overall_ok = False
            continue
        except RuntimeError as exc:
            print(f"{repo}: {_scrub(str(exc), private_name)}")
            overall_ok = False
            continue
        print(f"{repo}: refused forbidden probe, passed clean probe")

    return 0 if overall_ok else 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv))
